That's not a luckstone, it's a loadstone.  You've just discovered
everything you need to know about them.  They are very heavy, they
always curse themselves when you pick them up, and they otherwise
serve no purpose.  One version of the gnome minend level (the one you
found) has both a loadstone and a luckstone.  The only real way to
tell them apart without picking one up is to try to kick it.  A
loadstone will only move when kicked by something with extraordinarily
high strength, and then only one space.  A luckstone, being much
lighter, will move a lot further.

